            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0595" n="569" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v19/pg569"/>

                <head>287. Memorandum From Robert W.
                        Komer of the National Security Council Staff to the President’s
                    Special Assistant for National Security Affairs (Bundy)<anchor n="0" xml:id="d287-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-05-02">May 2,
                    1963</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">McGB:</p>
                <p>Re President’s desire to freeze any AID
                    announcements on Pakistan because of chilly Pak
                    reception for Rusk, consortium due to
                    announce tomorrow agreement on $400 million 1963-4 aid to Paks (200 ours).</p>
                <pb facs="0596" n="570" xml:id="pg570"/>
                <p>Bill Gaud says hard to see how we could stop announcement since other countries
                    involved. I’ve noted Ayub was very nice
                    to Rusk (Karachi Secto 30)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d287-f2"/> and Paks, who want $550 million won’t be elated over
                    announcement so I’ve ok’d Bill going ahead (I see no other choice).</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">RWK</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
